attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 2, `cydC` to `infA`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 91 to 100% of them, fewest at column 1, `aat`, 91% {S1}.

@variable **A long variable stretch follows**, columns 3 to 39, carried by 78 to 89%, [[arginine transport]] at columns 22 to 26 and [[putrescine transport]] at columns 29 to 32 {S2.c3-39, Q}. A branch of 9 shell families runs through columns 40 to 48, [[phage tail]], carried by 15 to 26% {S2.b40}. Then columns 54 to 57, `gsiD` to `gsiA`, are [[glutathione transport]], and a branch of 17 shell families runs through columns 54 to 70 {S2.c54-57, S2.b54, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.04 against 0.44 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 49, `yliI`, is a variable column, at 1.07 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 76 to 78, `glnH` to `glnQ`, are [[glutamine transport]], carried by 44 to 35% {S2.c76-78, Q}. The last column is `ybiO`, in 30% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 91% of genes**, 0.43 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.58 against 0.17 bits, and names fewer genes, 71% against 96% {C}.

